  "an8.20:2.6": "_Uddhastaṁ aruṇaṁ, nandimukhī ratti_ is very idiomatic, and _nandimukhi_ is generally treated as “face”. The idiom is surprisingly not used in this sense in Skt. But some Skt uses of the term are for a son of Rudra, suggesting that here _mukha_ is “cause”, i.e. “bringer of joy”. I take uddhasta as related to uddacca. ",
